<http://data.silknow.org/object/2fd64420-b365-329a-8ca1-37b7032ada2a/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Stevengraph picture woven in silk and mounted on card. Portrait of jockey Tom Cannon wearing Lord Rosebery's racing colours consisting of a jacket branded in rose and primrose hoops and rose coloured cap against a shaded white background. A facsimile of Cannon's signature is below on the right of the picture. On the front of the cream-coloured mount is 'Tom Cannon' and 'Woven in pure silk by T. Stevens, Coventry'. On the reverse of the mount is a trade label with a list of other Stevengraphs printed in 1887."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/2fd64420-b365-329a-8ca1-37b7032ada2a> .

